    <p>The 85mm f/1.8 is the single most recommended portrait and interview lens across the industry, and for good reason. It gives noticeably more background compression than a 50mm, so a busy office or a cluttered bookshelf turns into a soft wash of color and shape behind your subject, while the face itself renders with almost no perspective distortion at all.</p>
    <p><strong>DOP's take:</strong> If your interview setup has a fixed, comfortable amount of room — a dedicated studio corner, a rented space, a proper backdrop — this is the lens I would reach for over the 50mm every time. The one caveat: you need genuine distance (8-10 feet minimum) to frame a tight shot, so measure your space before buying. If your room is small, a 50mm will actually serve you better despite the less dramatic compression.</p>
    <div class="pc-grid">
      <div class="pc-box pro"><h4>Pros</h4><ul>
        <li>Best-in-class facial compression and flattery</li>
        <li>Beautiful, creamy background separation</li>
